      "message": "Note: as explained in the commit log footer, I\u0027ve switched to `find_vma()` instead of `vma_lookup()` in this backport. The reason being that vma_lookup() doesn\u0027t exist in v5.10. The problem with `find_vma()` is that it can sometimes return the \"next\" vma, so typically one needs to check `if (addr \u003c vma-\u003evm_start)`. In this case we are fine since we check the vma returned by find_vma() against our cached alloc-\u003evma pointer.",
